\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What SCL{} sees just before its decision for frame 101: a histogram of the candidates of the last 10 frames. Bottom axis: the logit of the detector score; top axis: the same position as a score; height: the number of candidates. Dashed line: first split $t_1$; solid line: second split $t_2$. Light bars: background (below $t_1$); hatched bars: uncertain (between the splits); dark bars: confident (above $t_2$). $\rho $: the share of confident candidates in the foreground; the median of $\rho $ decides the mode. (a) MOT17-02 with YOLOX-X: most foreground candidates are confident (median $\rho \ge 0.5$), so the stream is clean. (b) KITTI 0001 with RT-DETR-L: many are uncertain (median $\rho <0.5$), so the stream is noisy}}{6}{figure.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:groups}{{2}{6}{What \scl {} sees just before its decision for frame 101: a histogram of the candidates of the last 10 frames. Bottom axis: the logit of the detector score; top axis: the same position as a score; height: the number of candidates. Dashed line: first split $t_1$; solid line: second split $t_2$. Light bars: background (below $t_1$); hatched bars: uncertain (between the splits); dark bars: confident (above $t_2$). $\rho $: the share of confident candidates in the foreground; the median of $\rho $ decides the mode. (a) MOT17-02 with YOLOX-X: most foreground candidates are confident (median $\rho \ge 0.5$), so the stream is clean. (b) KITTI 0001 with RT-DETR-L: many are uncertain (median $\rho <0.5$), so the stream is noisy}{figure.25}{}}
